# Catppuccin Mocha High Contrast
# Catppuccin Mocha with the range opened up at both ends: the dark ramp is
# about a quarter darker, so the terminal sits deeper, and text, dim text and
# the surfaces that draw borders are lifted. The accent hues are Mocha's own —
# only the two that draw the focused border are brightened, because a gradient
# that reads as a light source has to be lighter than what it sits on.
#
# The dark roles move together. crust < mantle < base is load-bearing: the bar,
# the panels and the windows are layered with them, and darkening base alone
# would flatten that.
#
# Roles, darkest background to brightest accent. Every themed config is
# rendered from exactly these keys — see hypr/scripts/theme.sh.
name = Catppuccin Mocha High Contrast
mode = dark

crust     = 0c0c14
mantle    = 12121c
base      = 161622
surface0  = 4f5169   # inactive window border, and waybar panel fill
surface1  = 636680   # inactive workspace digits; also the terminal's ANSI black
overlay   = 8c91a8   # the dimmest readable text
subtext   = c0c7de
text      = e2e9fc
rosewater = f5e0dc
red       = f38ba8
peach     = fab387
yellow    = f9e2af
green     = a6e3a1
teal      = 94e2d5
sapphire  = 74c7ec
blue      = a0c5fd   # focused border, lighter half of the gradient
lavender  = c6cdfe
mauve     = d8bafa   # focused border, and the highlight colour
pink      = f5c2e7
